# PCA Parent Web - environment configuration example
# Copy to .env (local dev) or .env.production (production build) and adjust.

# Base URL of the future PCA backend HTTP API. The browser NEVER talks to
# MySQL directly -- only through this typed HTTP boundary.
VITE_PCA_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4001

# Demo/fixture mode. When true, all data comes from clearly-labelled
# DEVELOPMENT_ONLY synthetic fixtures via the dev implementations of the
# typed API client interfaces (see src/api/dev). Must default to false in
# any production build.
VITE_PCA_DEMO_MODE=true

# OPTIONAL -- leave unset unless this deployment genuinely publishes one.
#
# Absolute http(s) URL where THIS deployment publishes the PCA Child App for
# Android. No example host is given here on purpose: an invented value would be
# a fabricated or dead download link on the parent console's most prominent
# action, and there is no app-store URL or APK artifact anywhere in this
# repository to point at. Do not put a Google Play address here unless the app
# is actually published there.
#
# There is no default and no fallback. A value whose scheme is anything other
# than http or https -- javascript:, data:, a bare hostname -- is treated as
# unset by src/config/env.ts and never reaches an href.
#
# Unset is a supported, fully-working state, NOT a broken one: the header's
# "Download App" action is always visible either way, and the internal
# /download page it opens then states plainly that no Android download is
# configured for this environment. iOS is post-V1 and has no variable here.
# VITE_PCA_ANDROID_APP_DOWNLOAD_URL=
